<title>INDIA: India forex market inactive as Bombay banks closed.</title>
<headline>India forex market inactive as Bombay banks closed.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange market was inactive as banks in Bombay, the main commercial centre, were closed for a Moslem holiday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The rupee closed at 35.79/80 against the dollar on Thursday, up from 35.80/81 opening, and at its strongest level for four months.</p>
<p>The six month annualised premium closed at 4.97 percent compared to the previous close of 5.75 percent, they said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
